IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch12-16`

-- Tests for chapters 12 to 16.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (12.1, 14.4 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.

§ `Tests -- chapters 12 to 16`

§§ `12.1 -- the three occasions`

-- 12.1: arguments are levy, purpose, an aid for the eldest daughter's marriage has been levied before.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid `making the eldest son a knight` FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` FALSE
-- "once": a second aid for the same marriage is not the one occasion.
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE)
-- Fork F12: the exception is read as reaching aids only, so a scutage for a named purpose still needs counsel.
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 12 -- the levy is an aid for one of the three purposes` Scutage `ransoming the person` FALSE)
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` Scutage `ransoming the person` FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 12 -- the levy needs the common counsel of the kingdom` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE)

§§ `12.1 to 12.2 -- when a scutage or aid may be imposed`

-- Arguments: levy, purpose, daughter's aid levied before, imposed by common counsel, no more than a reasonable aid.
-- The three occasions need no common counsel, but the aid must be reasonable.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- 12.2 "for these": the limit holds even where there was common counsel.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `making the eldest son a knight` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `making the eldest son a knight` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Any other aid: common counsel is needed; 12.2 does not speak of its size.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- A scutage always needs common counsel (fork F12).
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Scutage `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Scutage `ransoming the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- "once marrying": an aid for the same marriage a second time is no longer one of the three.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- 12.3: "In like manner it shall be done concerning aids from the citizens of London."
-- Arguments: purpose, daughter's aid levied before, imposed by common counsel, reasonable.
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` `some other purpose` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` `ransoming the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred

§§ `Chapter 13 -- liberties and free customs`

#ASSERT `ch 13 -- the citizens of London have all their ancient liberties and free customs, by land and by water` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 13 -- the citizens of London have all their ancient liberties and free customs, by land and by water` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 13 -- all other cities, boroughs, towns and ports have all their liberties and free customs` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 13 -- all other cities, boroughs, towns and ports have all their liberties and free customs` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `Chapter 14 -- the summons`

-- 14.1-14.3: a scutage, or an aid other than the three cases, needs common counsel, so the King must summon.
-- expect: MUST `cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal`
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal` Scutage `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal` AT 3
-- "except in the three cases aforesaid": no summons duty for an aid for ransoming the King.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons to be summoned by letters under seal` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: MUST `cause all others who hold of the King in chief to be summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs, for a fixed date after at least forty days and at a fixed place`
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause all others who hold of him in chief to be summoned generally` Scutage `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause all others who hold of him in chief to be summoned generally` Aid `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `cause all others who hold of the King in chief to be summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs, for a fixed date after at least forty days and at a fixed place` AT 3
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will cause all others who hold of him in chief to be summoned generally` Aid `making the eldest son a knight` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: MUST `specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons`
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons` Scutage `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons` Scutage `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons` AT 3
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 14 -- the King will specify the reason of the summons in all letters of summons` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

-- 14.2: "after the expiry of at least forty days".
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the least number of days between the summons and the date fixed` EQUALS 40
-- Arguments: greater tenants summoned by letters, others summoned generally, days to the date fixed, a place fixed, reason in every letter.
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 90 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 39 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` FALSE TRUE 60 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE FALSE 60 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 60 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 60 TRUE FALSE)

-- 14.4: "although not all who were summoned have come".
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 15 -- aids taken by lords`

-- 15.1: arguments are purpose, an aid for the daughter's marriage levied before.
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `ransoming the person` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `making the eldest son a knight` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `once marrying the eldest daughter` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `once marrying the eldest daughter` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `some other purpose` FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 15 -- the King will not grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants, except for the three purposes` `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `grant a licence to take an aid from his own free tenants` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `grant a licence to take an aid from his own free tenants`
#TRACE `ch 15 -- the King will not grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants, except for the three purposes` `some other purpose` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 15 -- the King will not grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants, except for the three purposes` `ransoming the person` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `grant a licence to take an aid from his own free tenants` AT 2
-- 15.2: arguments are purpose, daughter's aid levied before, no more than a reasonable aid.
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the aid levied by a lord on one of the three occasions may be this aid` `ransoming the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the aid levied by a lord on one of the three occasions may be this aid` `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 15 -- the aid levied by a lord on one of the three occasions may be this aid` `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 16 -- service for a knight's fee`

-- 16.1: arguments are a knight's fee or free tenement, service demanded, service due.
#ASSERT `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` TRUE 10 10 EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` TRUE 11 10 EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` TRUE 9 10 EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` FALSE 11 10 EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- assertions written: 52.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
